From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JetBox build <build@jetbox.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:37:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] jetbox: management mask and privileged removal of foreign
 profiles

Changing the management URL (SetConfig, Login) to a host outside
*<AllowedManagementSuffix> now requires a privileged caller, regardless of
the SSH server state. The suffix is a build-time value in jetboxbrand; empty
keeps the upstream behaviour.

RemoveProfile of a profile that belongs to another OS user or has been
registered, and Logout of a profile that is not active or belongs to another
user, require a privileged caller. Registration is tracked per profile with
<id>.registered (written on a successful login) and <id>.added (written by
AddProfile); a profile without <id>.added predates the marks and is treated
as registered.
